cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the paper and this deposit."
type: software
title: >-
  Code and run records for "Bearing Fault Detection by Event-Time Phase
  Coherence with a Shaft-Harmonic Veto and a Geometry Margin Rule"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-23
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24462231
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nermen-Salama/ECAC-Bearing-Fault-Detection"
authors:
  - family-names: Salama
    given-names: Nermen
    email: nermen.salama@h-eng.helwan.edu.eg
  - family-names: Bassiuny
    given-names: A. M.
  - family-names: Tolba
    given-names: A. S.
  - family-names: Meligy
    given-names: Rowida
keywords:
  - bearing fault detection
  - phase coherence
  - Rayleigh test
  - envelope analysis
  - condition monitoring
abstract: >-
  Training-free bearing fault detector (version A15) based on the phase
  coherence of impact-event times at the kinematic fault frequencies, with a
  half-integer shaft-harmonic veto and a geometry margin rule, together with
  the kurtogram envelope-comb comparator, the scoring and test scripts, and
  the per-record run files behind every result in the paper.
